{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>וירח.</b> On the pattern of \"וינח בכל גבול מצרים\" (Exodus 10:14), and the resh is vocalized [with no dagesh] because the het is a guttural letter, according to the rule of the sacred language. Far be it, far be it that HaShem smells, and He does not eat, for thus it is written: \"אשר חלב זבחימו יאכלו\" (Deuteronomy 32:38). Rather the meaning is that He accepted the burnt offering, and it was pleasing before Him, like a person who smells a pleasant fragrance and it is agreeable to him:" "<b>הניחוח.</b> From the root of מנוחה, and the het is doubled like the doubling of פא and נאפופיה, and the meaning is that He rested [from] the fragrance of wrath, or that a supernal force rests:" "<b>אל לבו.</b> Like 'with His heart,' and afterward He revealed His secret to Noah, for he was a prophet." "And the meaning of 'I will never again curse' is as He cursed by means of man, for thus it is written: 'cursed is the ground.'" "יצר. It is the offspring that is formed for him:" "ולא אוסיף עוד. Concerning the flood." "And the word 'עוד' [means] forever or a second time, and likewise 'ויבך על צואריו עוד' (Genesis 46:29)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:56.001809787Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}